# The APK (~98 MB) is kept OUT of git on purpose — it would sit in history
# permanently, close to GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, and every clone would pull it.
#
# This does NOT break the download button: .vercelignore exists and takes
# precedence for `vercel` CLI deploys, and it deliberately does not list the APK,
# so the file still reaches the deployment from the local working tree.
#
# The one case that breaks is deploying through Vercel's GitHub integration — the
# APK is not in the repo, so /drikr.apk would 404. If you switch to that, upload
# the binary as a GitHub Release asset and point APK.url in lib/site.ts at it.
public/*.apk

# Local project links written by tooling — machine-specific, not source.
.xcelit
